<component type="desktop">
  <id>cc.etke.komai</id>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">@KOMAI_DESKTOP_ID@.desktop</launchable>
  <replaces>
    <id>cc.etke.komai</id>
  </replaces>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <developer id="cc.etke">
    <name>Komai</name>
  </developer>
  <name>Komai</name>
  <summary>A Matrix chat app you can get to love</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Komai is a desktop-first Matrix chat application built with Rust, C++ and QML. It is optimized for large screens, with comfortably readable text, larger hit targets, and a keyboard-driven workflow designed for productivity.</p>
    <p>Komai began as a usability-focused fork of nheko, but has since been heavily rebuilt around the Rust matrix-sdk runtime and a growing Rust core.</p>
    <p>Features include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Matrix messaging with end-to-end encryption support</li>
      <li>Voice and video calls</li>
      <li>File, image, audio and emoji messages with a built-in media viewer</li>
      <li>Replies, threads, and message forwarding</li>
      <li>Multi-account support via dedicated application profiles</li>
      <li>10+ built-in themes meeting WCAG AA contrast guidelines, plus user-themable support</li>
      <li>30+ languages</li>
      <li>Keyboard-driven workflow with Vim-style shortcuts</li>
      <li>Local automation via Model Context Protocol (MCP), CLI commands, and D-Bus</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Komai is fully Free Software (GPL-3.0-or-later), with no CLA and no contributor gatekeeping.</p>
  </description>
